Subject: Describe the Bluetooth UART sleep states on SM-G955N

The Samsung UART suspend and resume callbacks select btsleep and
btdefault for ttySAC1. The Korean SM-G955N DT only supplies default,
rts and tx_dat, so both lookups fail on every system suspend cycle.
Expose the SoC's existing Bluetooth sleep group on this board and
alias btdefault to the original active pin group. Keep the existing
RTS and TX-data mappings.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lte_kor_10.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lte_kor_10.dts
@@ -321 +321,7 @@ &pd_dpu0 {
 };
+
+&serial_1 {
+	pinctrl-names = "default", "rts", "tx_dat", "btdefault", "btsleep";
+	pinctrl-3 = <&uart1_bus>;
+	pinctrl-4 = <&uart1_btsleep>;
+};
